<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="45136" href="schedule/2007/spring/AIS/490/45136.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2007" href="schedule/2007.xml">2007</calendarYear><term id="120071" href="schedule/2007/spring.xml">Spring 2007</term><subject id="AIS" href="schedule/2007/spring/AIS.xml">American Indian Studies</subject><course id="490" href="schedule/2007/spring/AIS/490.xml">Adv Topics in Am Ind Studies</course></parents><sectionNumber>E3 </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>History of Am Ind Education</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>In this course, we will study the perceived need to 'civilize' American Indians through educational initiatives from colonial times to the present day. Topics include mission schools, government boarding schools, and tribally run high schools and tribal colleges. Contact the instructor (debreese@uiuc.edu) for information regarding texts and readings for the course.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign. </sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2007-01-16Z</startDate><endDate>2007-05-02Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>12:00 PM</start><end>02:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>W      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>59A</roomNumber><buildingName>English Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Reese" firstName="D">Reese, D</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>